+  // Patch 0901. Off by default, which is one line and two separate wins.
+  //
+  // It is the last endpoint the browser still contacts on its own with Fury's
+  // launch flags, and it contacts it on every download: the client report goes
+  // to a hardcoded sb-ssl.google.com URL, not through anything an API key gates.
+  // For a browser whose entire premise is that traffic leaves through the
+  // profile's proxy and nowhere else, a per-download ping to Google is the
+  // deviation, whatever it is called.
+  //
+  // And it removes a contradiction that was already there. With
+  // --disable-background-networking the Safe Browsing database never downloads
+  // (v4_update_protocol_manager.cc:106-109), so the browser has been protecting
+  // nothing while chrome://settings reported Standard protection and while the
+  // download pings kept going out. Off is the honest state, and it is the state
+  // the settings page will now describe.
+  //
+  // The pref rather than the URL constant, deliberately:
+  // download_protection_delegate_desktop.cc CHECKs the constructed URL is valid,
+  // so blanking the constant crashes the browser at startup. The pref is also
+  // the single gate that client-side phishing detection, the ping manager,
+  // notification telemetry and password protection all read — one flag, one
+  // vector, no traffic.
+  //
+  // A DEFAULT, which is what this registration sets. A profile whose Preferences
+  // file already carries safebrowsing.enabled keeps its own value; Fury creates
+  // profiles fresh, so the default is what every new one gets, and that is the
+  // case this has to be right for.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kSafeBrowsingEnabled, true,
+      prefs::kSafeBrowsingEnabled, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
